from περιρραίνω; perirranth/rion, ou, to/, 
0I. an utensil for besprinkling, or a vessel for lustral water, Lat. aspergillum, Hdt.
0II. περιρραντήρια ἀγορᾶς the parts of the forum sprinkled with lustral water, Lex ap. Aeschin.

from πικρός; pikro/ths, htos, h(, 
0I. pungency, bitterness, of taste, Plat.
0II. metaph. bitterness, cruelty, Hdt., Eur.

from πλεονεκτέω; pleone/kthma, atos, to/, 
0I. an advantage, gain, privilege, Plat., Dem.: in pl. gains, successes, Xen.
0II. an act of overreaching, selfish trick, Dem.

from προνωπής; pronw/pia, wn, ta/, 
0I. the front of a house (cf. ἐνώπια), Eur.: metaph. in sg., χώρας Πελοπίας πρ., of Troezen, the outer portal of Peloponnesus, id.
0II. as adj. in front, before the door, id.

from προσικνέομαι; prosi/ktwr, oros, o(, 
0I. one that comes to a god, a suppliant, Aesch.
0II. pass. he to whom one comes as a suppliant, a protector, of a god, id.

